F5-TTS over Chatterbox: Chatterbox pins torch==2.6/transformers==5.2 and can't share the venv with WhisperX (torch~=2.8, hub<1.0); F5 installs with current pins and supports exact output length (fix_duration), which dubbing needs. CC-BY-NC weights accepted for now. Reference text is romanized because F5's tokenizer only knows Latin/Chinese: Japanese text scored WER 0.47 (leaked Japanese-like sounds), English translation of the ref 0.61 (repeated ref words), romaji 0.34; leakage that remained came from a reference ending mid-sentence (...desukedo), hence the complete-sentence preference and ending the ref on one (WER 0.03 on full run). ASR verification + seed retry exists because 1-word lines vary wildly by seed ('Japan?' -> 'Depends.'/'Mr. Payne.'). MIN_DURATION 0.8 s: 0.5-0.6 s slots garbled; overrun is left to #6 via gap_after.
